Based on my thorough independent verification, I can now issue the verdict. Key findings from my research:

**Verified correct:**
- OA-WAM camera score: **80.5%** on LIBERO-Plus Table 2 (confirmed from paper HTML)
- CKT-WAM camera score: **77.4%** on LIBERO-Plus Table 1 (confirmed)
- Motus camera score: **21.6%**, unperturbed **87.0%**, overall **71.5%** on RoboTwin 2.0-Plus (confirmed from arXiv:2603.22078 full HTML)
- Motus **NOT** evaluated on LIBERO-Plus in arXiv:2603.22078 (confirmed)
- LIBERO-Plus public code confirmed at github.com/sylvestf/LIBERO-plus
- Motus checkpoint public at motus-robotics/Motus (confirmed)
- ReViWo ICLR 2025 exists with public code (confirmed)
- No VQ-Perceiver style concurrent work found
- OpenVLA-OFT dual-camera wrist confound confirmed by LIBERO-Plus paper's own ablations

**New findings:**
- ViPRA (arXiv:2511.07732, ICLR 2026): "jointly predicts future visual tokens and latent actions using VQ-VAE" — not in proposal's landscape, though different target (joint prediction quality, not camera robustness)
- The 56.4% OpenVLA-OFT figure (cited as "CKT-WAM Table 1") may need source verification — more likely from the LIBERO-Plus paper directly

